WEBVTT

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:13.290
Miss Minare, regardless of the fact that when
Manager returns you'll most likely get fired,

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.450
you're saying that you're going to quit?

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.250
Hey, Mr. Mato. Do you have a minute?

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:22.000
I've been meaning to ask--

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.540
what's my salary for talking on the radio
for 20 minutes four times per month?

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.080
Ah, I figured it'd be around that.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.790
No, it's all good. Sorry to bother you. Bye.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.540
Of course not!

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:36.580
Ah, what a relief.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.950
Please don't scare us like that.

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:09.370
"Dream Space of Bread and Curry VOYAGER"

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:10.500
"Dream Space of Bread and Curry VOYAGER"
Good night!

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:14.290
Good night! We'll see you tomorrow.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:17.040
"Episode 6: There's No Such Thing"

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.290
"Episode 6: There's No Such Thing"
What did I expect?

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:23.290
I'm the one who kept dodging
Nakahara's advances.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:27.500
I have no right to be jealous.
Well, not that I am.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.160
But it's all good.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.700
Mr. Mato said so, too.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:38.950
Just wait, Minare. Pretty soon, thousands
of people will be dying to hear your voice.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:40.450
"*He never said that."

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.830
Oh! Speak of the devil.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.450
You're responsible for
coming up with the next idea.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:50.950
What? I am? You gotta be kidding me.

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:54.580
Ah, hello. Mr. Mato?
About that next broadcast...

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.700
Huh? Who is this?

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:00.410
What do you mean, who's this?
You're the one who called, Minare.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.660
D-Dad?!

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:03.660
Shoot, I called the wrong number.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.370
Anyway, I heard your radio show.
The late-night one.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.910
What? But how? I never told you.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.370
A friend told me about it.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:10.660
"Pachinko Himawari"

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:14.450
"Pachinko Himawari"
Well, I gotta say. I thought it was great.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:15.950
"Pachinko Himawari"
But it got weird at the end.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.790
"Pachinko Himawari"
Aliens? Come on, you an idiot?

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:21.040
Beats me. I feel the same way about it.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:24.620
So, what? You're going to be a radio DJ now?

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:27.330
What happened to your apprenticeship
with the acupuncturist?

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:28.790
Oh, um...

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:33.200
Dad, that was just a white lie I told
as an excuse to move to Sapporo.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.620
I'm still deciding what to do.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:39.660
It's unclear what the director
actually thinks of me.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:42.370
I see.

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:45.830
It reeks of alcohol through my phone.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:47.000
Minare.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.000
Huh?

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.290
Take up any job you want.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.790
Just be the one who everybody laughs at.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.700
That's the most important thing.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.830
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:58.660
It's getting chilly, so I'm going home.

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:03.370
Agh. I'd rather not. How do I explain
the 40,000 yen I just lost?

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:10.160
The bright and divine-looking moon
from a second ago just faded away...

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.000
It doesn't matter!

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:16.540
Hey, Mr. Mato? About that next broadcast idea...

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:20.580
What? Nakahara? What's going on
with my phone today?

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:23.000
Watch out! Here comes the giraffe!

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.830
--Roar!
--How is that a giraffe?

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:27.000
You're doing great.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:30.450
Far better than the pre-school teacher
who's the worst at playing with children.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.200
Oh... Thank you.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.830
Was that a compliment?

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:37.000
All right. Let's go to sleep after we eat this.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.790
Meiko, you should go back home to your husband.

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:41.790
Cut him some slack.
He just went to a hostess bar.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:44.080
No! He went to the one
where he can touch the girls!

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:46.200
I won't forgive him unless he apologizes
and bows down to me

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.040
until he makes a hole in the ground.
Damn husband.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.000
Ah, jeez. I can't focus.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.410
I have to think of segment
ideas for Miss Minare.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:55.040
For her radio program?

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.580
Yeah, right. You already moved on
to playing games on your phone.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:04:59.910
U-Ugh...

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:01.910
Sorry.

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:02.750
Huh?

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:05.080
I'm sure you thought you'd be alone with him.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:07.040
What? Oh, um...

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.120
No...

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:11.790
This is just my intuition as his sister...

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:18.450
But if I did go back to my husband, knowing
Chuya, he would send you home, too.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.750
Yes, you're right.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.040
He's that kind of person.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:26.080
Your younger brother is a
serious and generous person.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:28.370
Oh, stop it.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:30.250
Do you have any siblings?

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:32.370
I have an older brother.

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:36.200
His only similarity to
Mr. Chuya is that he's serious.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.620
Otherwise, he's completely different.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:43.120
You weren't too talkative yesterday.
But how about tonight?

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.160
Six years ago...

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:52.700
Everything changed when
my parents died in the mountains.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:56.330
He was always the over-protective type
when it came to me.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:06:01.200
But not even five days after the incident, he
claimed that our parents appeared in his dream

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:05.950
and told him to risk his life to protect me.

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:11.750
Ever since then, I was placed in total
isolation--just like Kaspar Hauser.

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:14.290
Not only did he ban me from
going to school or seeing friends,

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:21.330
he locked me up in a room and didn't allow me
to use my phone unless I got his permission.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:24.120
I was eventually forced to quit university.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:27.040
So I had no choice but to
listen to Open University.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:30.660
No offense, but your brother
is a little crazy...

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.040
He's totally crazy.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:36.580
In the midst of that,
he got into a car accident.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:40.160
And when I learned that
a restaurant owner was involved,

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.580
I immediately strategized
a way for me to get out.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:48.160
As the perpetrator, he wouldn't
be able to say no if I requested

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:54.040
to go help out the restaurant to make amends.

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:56.620
I took advantage of someone's misfortune.

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:58.330
I'm the worst.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:01.750
No, I would do the same. I don't blame you.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:05.910
Plus, it all worked out.
The restaurant needed your help.

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:10.080
Anyway, I wonder what your
brother wants to do, ultimately.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:12.540
Mr. Chuya told me,

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:14.830
"I don't know what your brother told you,

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:20.580
but if he continues to obey your parents like
this, their words will become like a curse."

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:22.950
Just so you know, when Chuya
spits out cheesy lines like that,

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:25.620
it's most likely something from a TV drama.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:31.750
But while working at Voyager,
I found what I really want to do.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:36.290
Oh? What could it be?
A curry restaurant owner's wife?

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:41.080
Hey...

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:41.910
Yes?

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:46.910
Good, good. I'm grateful for Meiko's
bluntness in times like these.

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:52.330
In any case, I still need to come up with
a good idea for Miss Minare's program.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.160
Oh, Nakahara...

00:07:56.160 --> 00:08:00.450
I hope he's a little worried about me.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:06.660
Well this is a surprise. I've never
seen you look so sad before.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:09.080
This isn't a final farewell or anything.

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:11.330
A fellow soldier's setting out
on a new adventure.

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:14.000
I prefer that you send me off with a smile.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:15.660
I'm so excited.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.700
It's my first time overseas.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.620
I'll go check out that thing you mentioned.

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:21.540
Um, what was it called?

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:24.000
Oh yeah, <i>Monty Python</i>. That's right.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:28.410
I heard it on BBC but they're going to start
airing it in Japan, too, in the near future.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:30.330
Anyway, I have to get going.

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:34.000
I hope you use that. I used most
of my New Year's money for it.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:36.160
It's the latest model that just came out.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:39.330
It might be hard for you to use it though.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:43.580
Like always, you never understood
other people's feelings.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:46.330
The reason I'm sad is...

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:49.870
I know this is a dream about
what happened decades ago...

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:54.200
And that you're about to
be in a brutal accident...

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:57.080
Yeah! The Aramaki salmon.
Could you not send me four of them?

00:08:57.080 --> 00:09:00.830
It doesn't fit in my fridge.
Ah, it was Dad? Of course it was.

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:04.330
We're not living in Showa times anymore,
dammit. He doesn't understand.

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:08.790
I can't give it to my neighbors knowing
it's not going to fit in their fridge.

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:11.160
Chilled mutton would've been
a thousand times better.

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:13.330
What? You sent that two years ago?

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:16.500
Really? Anyway, forget about the salmon.

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:22.950
So, when I opened the massive ball of packaging
material, I ended up with a musty radio.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:26.410
Oh, that thing. Your father
insisted that I send it to you.

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:28.950
How should I know what that's about.

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:33.830
Anyway, I heard the news.
You're doing radio now?

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:36.200
Why wouldn't you tell me
such an important thing?

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:40.040
Well, that's because it's not
really anything to brag about...

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:44.160
Income-wise, it's like why bother
having the Labor Standards Act...

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:48.540
But you still told your father.
It makes me sad. Oh, very sad.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:51.290
He didn't exactly hear from me, either.

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.750
Did he say anything?

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:58.330
What was it? Oh, yeah. Something like
"be the one who everyone laughs at."

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:00.950
Yup. That sounds like him.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:04.410
Minare.

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:07.540
Don't take a loser's words seriously.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:10.410
Live a life people can respect.

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:12.120
Understood?

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:16.120
It all feels disconcerting.

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:19.830
Oh, yeah. Here you go. The radio
program ideas you asked me to think of.

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:20.700
Nice.

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:23.580
I think they're all pretty good.

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:29.120
So, what do you think?

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:31.370
It was my fault for asking you.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:32.660
What?

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:35.250
Forget that I even asked!

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:38.080
What are you doing?

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:40.160
Every man to his trade.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:43.000
"To: Kanetsugu Mato
Do you know about this radio?"
Why don't you ask your father about it?

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:47.540
What? No way. That man's drunk half of the time.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.790
He's either in dirty joke-telling mode,
venting mode, or preaching mode,

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:52.450
or else he just goes off on random
tangents. He makes no sense at all.

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:54.040
You can't have a proper conversation with him.

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:56.750
I see. So, it runs in the family.

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:58.410
Oh? That was fast.

00:10:58.410 --> 00:10:58.950
Huh?

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:01.450
"From: Kanetsugu Mato
That's the Sky Sensor 5900.
Your father sent you a nice radio."

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:07.160
Will you elaborate on the "nice radio" part?

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:10.370
I'm about to do a live broadcast,
so we'll talk later. Call me after 10 PM.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:12.290
Dammit, this is unsettling.

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:13.870
So you like that radio, right?

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:17.040
The opposite. I have no interest
in it whatsoever,

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:19.580
and I was hoping I could sell it
for 1,000,000 yen or something.

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:21.910
Does she not have a heart?

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:25.450
Oh, yeah. I know who I can give this salmon to.

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:31.950
This neighbor's not home.
Oh, well. I'll just hang it here.

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:32.370
"This is for you."

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:34.330
"This is for you."
Who lives here?

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:37.750
A woman who looks like a college
student moved in here in April.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.700
I've never talked to her.

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:43.500
If I were this neighbor's boyfriend,
I'd call the police over this.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:46.200
Oh...

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:47.540
Excuse me.

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:49.750
Thank you for the other day.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:53.750
Oh... You're the woman
who called the police on me.

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:54.950
The police?

00:11:54.950 --> 00:11:56.120
How can I help you?

00:11:56.120 --> 00:12:00.000
Ah, please wait a second.
This thing is tangled on my fingers.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.950
Mr. Oki! Please accept this
without asking any questions.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:03.950
"Salmon"

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:06.950
"*The ultimate suspicious person."

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:10.750
Okay. I will.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:11.870
Anything else?

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:13.620
That's it from me.

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:20.000
Ah... That made me so distraught, it triggered
my first Valentine's memory in high school.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.160
It's like I forgot how to be "girly."

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:25.500
Miss Minare, Miss Minare. Something's wrong
with that guy, don't you think?

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:26.370
What?

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:29.580
Oh, you too? Glad it's not just me.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:33.700
Last time... Well, I caused him so
much trouble when I stayed here,

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:37.000
and it took him a while to recognize me.

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:41.330
I was shocked, to be honest.
Am I that forgettable?

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:43.910
I like to think I'm like the cheap version
of Mirei Kiritani when it comes to looks.

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:46.790
--I'm not talking about that.
--He must be gay.

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:50.120
Didn't you notice when he opened his door?

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:52.620
Something reeked out of his room.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:55.120
It's the smell of death.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.790
You watch way too many dramas, my friend.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:01.370
Do you even know what death smells like?
Have you smelled it before?

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:04.330
Well, you can call it the smell
of something rotting, too.

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:09.040
When protein deteriorates...
You know what it smells like?

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:11.080
It all smells fishy to me.

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:14.200
He had huge bags under his eyes.
He can't be right in the head.

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:18.370
Ah, sorry. I did notice something off about him.

00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:20.910
But since he has helped me in the past,

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:23.290
I was trying not to criticize him.

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:24.660
In any case...

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:28.830
If we pry and he responds, "Huh? You're the one
who reeks." Then it's game over right there.

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:30.040
Ugh! I reek of salmon!

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:35.040
Well, if it comes down to it, I'm sure you can
take him down by yourself, Miss Minare.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:38.080
But if anything happens, don't
hesitate to call me--even if it's late.

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:42.790
I'm done dealing with suspense and the occult.

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:47.870
That's it. I'll make my program
warm and fluffy like a towel.

00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:52.580
--Hey, Mizuho.
--Oh?

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:53.620
Miss Minare!

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:55.120
I come bearing gifts.

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:57.700
Wow! Thank you very much.

00:13:57.700 --> 00:14:00.950
--So, hey. Have you heard from Mr. Mato?
--Oh?

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:03.370
About the next episode of Wave, Listen to Me!

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:09.700
Yes, I said I would come up with ideas, too,
but I couldn't get it approved by Mr. Mato.

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:14.830
Ah! Someone save me from this labyrinth
with an Imabari towel-like, fluffy idea!

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.830
An Imabari towel...?

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:17.950
Oh...

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:19.910
Actually...

00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:22.330
We received a strange fax
addressed to you, Miss Minare.

00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:24.500
Really? Let's see it!

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:26.000
It's this.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:27.410
"I'm cursed. I think you'll understand.

00:14:27.410 --> 00:14:31.870
My girlfriend is dead
but she hasn't forgiven me.

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:34.620
I'll be dragged to the other side
if this goes on..."

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:36.580
What?

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:39.580
This is exactly what I don't want.

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:41.580
What is this?

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:44.080
Do you think he wants you to go to his place?

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:48.450
You mentioned how older listeners
still fax in their requests.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:50.040
It could be a senile old man.

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:52.500
I thought that at first, as well.

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:53.790
But as you can see...

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:55.410
Twenty-eight years old?

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.700
That pretty much confirms this is a prank.

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:59.410
This looks like it's from
an over-the-top horror movie

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:01.200
with this sloppy handwriting
and stains all over.

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:03.250
It has to be a prank, right?

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:06.370
Plus, this is about his "dead girlfriend"?
Very creative, dude.

00:15:06.370 --> 00:15:07.370
"Shinji Oki"
What?

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:09.750
Mizuho...

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:10.750
Huh?

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:15.120
This actually might be a serious inquiry.

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:16.450
What?

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:19.120
"Abbreviated"

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:22.410
Well, isn't this something?

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:27.040
If we could laugh it off like that,
we wouldn't need the Hokkaido Police!

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:29.950
Minare, about that second
episode segment idea...

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:33.120
Yes, sir. I knew you'd come save the day.

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:36.250
It doesn't have to be a live broadcast,
just so you know.

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:37.830
What?

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:41.080
So that's why... Here.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:45.750
Go visit the sender of the fax and record
the investigation from start to finish.

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:50.700
It's a rare thing to hear a genuinely
scared human voice on the radio.

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:53.830
Mr. Mato, I would understand
if it was just the first episode...

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:55.870
But if we continue on like this
for the second episode,

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:58.000
the listeners will think it's
an occult program!

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:00.910
Nanba, accompany Minare as an assistant.

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:02.620
What? Are you sure?

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:05.160
Ah, but I have the Cruise Nine broadcast.

00:16:05.160 --> 00:16:08.750
Just select the CDs for me
and I'll take care of the rest.

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:14.500
And also, if Minare chokes, I want you
to step up and talk to this guy.

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:15.410
What?!

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:17.580
I want to keep the recording as stock material.

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:19.500
Oh... This is intimidating.

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:21.410
I can't let this slide.

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:25.410
That's enough! This vicious power
harassment has got to stop!

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:28.870
Um, it's just a normal business order.

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:30.620
All right, Mizuho.

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:35.540
Let's go together. I forgot I vowed
to protect you no matter what.

00:16:35.540 --> 00:16:37.580
Th-Thank you very much.

00:16:37.580 --> 00:16:39.290
When did she do that?

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:40.120
Easy.

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:45.120
Mr. Mato, you deserve to contract
an unknown STD and die, seriously.

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:46.410
Minare.

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:49.450
You might be sick of hearing this,

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:53.830
but TV viewers are customers,
radio listeners are participants.

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:58.540
Even if a novice radio personality
messes up at a location,

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:02.950
that's material for listeners to talk
with us about in the next episode.

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:07.200
So, it's not wrong to say
we're reliant on our listeners.

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:10.160
And you're still pretty much an amateur.

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:12.500
Take full advantage of it.

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:15.910
Um, I get that you're trying
to make me feel better,

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:18.620
but I'm not worried about the complaints.

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:22.370
I'm concerned that the sender
of this fax is seriously insane.

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:25.450
If this were a proper company,
they would just ignore it.

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:28.950
Those who risk their lives for entertainment,
they're called professionals.

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:32.950
I know a radio personality
who isn't exactly like that.

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:37.620
Minare, just trust the director
who fell for you at first sight.

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:40.330
Should anything happen to you...

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:43.000
...I'll bail you out, I promise.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:47.950
Oh... So, you're assuming
that I'll get arrested. I see.

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:54.910
I'm excited to go on location
with you, Miss Minare!

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:56.580
I'm excited, too.

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:59.700
This mini is comfortable to ride in,
despite what I've heard.

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:02.910
We'll have you drive the mini
yourself eventually.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:06.200
But anyway, you're bringing
a camcorder for a radio broadcast?

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:08.620
Yes, I bring it with me every time.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:11.120
It can be used as content
for the station's blog.

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:13.410
It doubles as insurance for the recorder, too.

00:18:13.410 --> 00:18:16.540
Oh... What if we captured ghost footage?

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:21.000
My parents live in Otaki, so I go to Lake
Shikotsu every year when I go home for Obon.

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:23.200
But I was never able to capture any ghosts.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:28.120
How cute. She says she's nervous,
but she can't even contain her excitement.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:31.290
If we end up with ghost footage,
I'd be fine with that.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:39.250
But there's a chance we'll capture something
the police will want from us as evidence.

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:44.500
Ah! No! Somebody help!

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:47.450
What was that voice?

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:50.120
Yes.

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:53.750
This is Moiwayama Radio.
We spoke on the phone earlier.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:02.870
You're the one who called the police
and caused the Aramaki incident...

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:04.370
I just saw you six hours ago.

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:06.160
--The radio station sent me
to exterminate the evil spirit.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:07.750
--The police and salmon...?
--The radio station sent me
to exterminate the evil spirit.

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:10.910
What? Please wait a minute.

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:13.250
If you're here because of that fax...

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:17.370
You're Minare Koda,
that late night radio personality?

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:18.750
Mr. Oki.

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:21.910
Are you familiar with <i>kuchikamizake</i>?

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:24.790
It's saké made from thoroughly
chewing on ripened grains.

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:28.450
The enzymes of the saliva convert it into sugar.

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:34.250
In ancient Japan, the Ryukyus and Taiwan,
this saké was produced for religious rituals.

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:35.660
The interesting thing is...

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:40.620
It was the women, the shrine maiden
or virgin's duty to make this saké.

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:43.410
Rituals, saké, women...

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:46.580
These three elements cannot be separated.

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:48.580
So, Mr. Oki...

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:51.580
Don't you think it all makes sense now?

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:56.540
The one who'll appease the evil spirit
of your home is the very woman

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:59.080
who's been drunk at your doorstep?

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:02.080
If you say so, I understand.
Please come in.

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:05.750
He didn't bother to react to
that long-winded joke just now.

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:09.450
It only goes to show how deep
and immense his struggle is.

00:20:11.370 --> 00:20:13.160
--Miss Minare.
--Yeah?

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:15.160
You could've let me know he was an acquaintance.

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:19.040
Right... Actually, I used to live
diagonally above his place.

00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:19.660
What?

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:21.500
We're not that well-acquainted.

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:24.750
He's just carried me back
to my place multiple times

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:27.790
after I would black out at his
thinking it was mine. That's all.

00:20:27.790 --> 00:20:31.660
That's a big deal! And if that's the case,
he's a very generous person!

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:32.830
Mizuho, don't forget.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:37.290
No matter how good of a person he is,
he's a civilian and we're the media.

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:43.160
A beautiful radio DJ comes to the rescue
for a civilian. That's our approach, got it?

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:47.000
This is going to be crucial to establish
my relationship with my listeners.

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:48.750
I'm not going to sell myself short.

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:51.290
I can't even describe her nature...

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:52.500
Come in.

00:20:55.620 --> 00:20:56.660
Whoa.

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:05.200
So, according to your fax,
your girlfriend has passed away?

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:07.660
Um, may I roll the camera?

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:10.830
Sure, that's fine... Yes.

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:14.080
But she'll be coming here...

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.290
...soon.

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:16.540
What?

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:27.910
Whoa, what is this? It reeks!

00:21:27.910 --> 00:21:29.120
Ah...

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:39.080
What the...?! What the heck is that?!

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:41.160
Forgive me!

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:43.160
--I didn't want to lose you, either!

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:47.040
--Great, he went straight into panic
without any explanation.
--I didn't want to lose you, either!

00:21:47.040 --> 00:21:50.950
Miss Minare, I noticed this
the moment we stepped inside...

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:54.660
This smell... It's rotting meat!

00:21:54.660 --> 00:21:56.410
Bring it on!

00:21:56.410 --> 00:22:01.120
I'd take a bizarre crime scene
over the occult any day!

00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:03.540
Hello, Nakahara?

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:05.620
When I look back at this moment,

00:22:05.620 --> 00:22:08.040
I can see I wasn't prepared at all
for what was about to happen.

00:22:08.040 --> 00:22:11.120
Nobody could've foreseen that
we were about to see a conclusion

00:22:11.120 --> 00:22:14.160
that was beyond all imagination.

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:44.540
"Next Episode"

00:23:44.540 --> 00:23:45.700
"Next Episode"
A countless number of amulets,
a suspicious vase,

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:48.830
"Preview"
A countless number of amulets,
a suspicious vase,

00:23:48.830 --> 00:23:52.410
"Preview"
a black liquid that reeks of rotten meat,

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:55.080
"Preview"
and a haggardly man's wailing...

00:23:55.080 --> 00:23:59.870
"Preview"
When the Onmyoji proceeds into
the darkness, into the swarm of flies...

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:01.540
"Preview"
Minare witnesses...

00:24:01.540 --> 00:24:08.330
"Preview"
The true form of the pieces of meat rotting
away, dripping jet black putrid juices...

00:24:08.330 --> 00:24:12.120
Next, on <i>Wave, Listen to Me!</i>: "I Want to Cry."

00:24:12.120 --> 00:24:14.000
Perish, evil spirit!

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:16.950
"See you next time!"
"Illustrated by Hiroaki Samura"
